{
  "analysis": "We are in /app with an empty-ish workspace and no project created yet. The task requires creating a new Python package named `mathutils` using a `pyproject.toml` configured to use the `uv_build` backend (PEP 732 editable-build mechanism), building it with `uv build`, installing it in editable mode with `uv pip install --editable .`, and verifying that code changes reflect immediately without reinstalling.",
  "plan": "1) Check that `uv` is available. 2) Create a standard `src/`-layout package `mathutils` with an `add(a,b)` function. 3) Write `pyproject.toml` using `uv_build` as the build backend. 4) Create a virtual environment with `uv venv`. 5) Run `uv build` to build sdists/wheels. 6) Install editable with `uv pip install --editable .`. 7) Verify import and function call. 8) Modify source and re-run the import/call to confirm editable install updates without reinstalling.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /app\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv --version\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "rm -rf mathutils\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p mathutils/src/mathutils\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > mathutils/src/mathutils/__init__.py <<'PY'\n\"\"\"mathutils: tiny math utilities.\"\"\"\n\nfrom .core import add\n\n__all__ = [\"add\"]\nPY\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > mathutils/src/mathutils/core.py <<'PY'\ndef add(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Add two numbers together.\"\"\"\n    return a + b\nPY\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > mathutils/pyproject.toml <<'TOML'\n[project]\nname = \"mathutils\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"Tiny math utilities\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.9\"\n\n[build-system]\n# Use uv's build backend (PEP 732 editable-build mechanism)\nrequires = [\"uv-build\"]\nbuild-backend = \"uv_build\"\nTOML\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > mathutils/README.md <<'MD'\n# mathutils\n\nA tiny example package.\nMD\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd mathutils\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv venv\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "source .venv/bin/activate\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv build\n",
      "duration": 3.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "uv pip install --editable .\n",
      "duration": 3.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python -c \"import mathutils; print(mathutils.add(2, 3))\"\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "perl -0777 -i -pe 's/return a \\+ b/return a + b + 100/' src/mathutils/core.py\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python -c \"import mathutils; print(mathutils.add(2, 3))\"\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The `mathutils` package was created with a `src/` layout and an `add` function. `pyproject.toml` is configured to use `uv_build` with `requires = [\"uv-build\"]`. A virtualenv was created, `uv build` successfully produced sdist and wheel, and `uv pip install --editable .` installed the package. Importing `mathutils` and calling `add(2,3)` returned 5, then after modifying the source to add 100, it returned 105 without reinstalling—confirming editable behavior works.",
  "plan": "The task requirements are satisfied. Optionally, we can show the key files (`pyproject.toml` and source) and list the dist artifacts as evidence, but no further changes are necessary.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la dist\n",
